# TASK 9b for Usher: fix a race condition in app/index.html.

The module script imports dom-accessibility-api from jsdelivr, so it runs only after that download. The iframe loads the local demo page faster, so its 'load' event has usually already fired before frame.addEventListener('load', ...) is attached (around line 1763). Result: on first open, the auto-scan never runs and the axe score never appears.

Fix: move the body of that load handler into a named function, e.g. onPageReady(). Attach it as the load listener as now, AND immediately after attaching it, check whether the iframe has already loaded (frame.contentDocument && frame.contentDocument.readyState === 'complete' && frame.contentDocument.location.href !== 'about:blank') and, if so, call onPageReady() straight away. Make sure it cannot run twice for the same load.

Check the other two frame 'load' listeners (around lines 1803 and 2615) for the same problem and apply the same pattern if needed.

Then confirm: opening app/ fresh shows the transcript filled and the axe score ("29 problems") without clicking anything.

